opment version. To confirm this, you have three options:\n173\t\n174\t1. Update Black's version if a newer release exists: `pip install -U black`\n175\t2. Use the online formatter at <https://black.vercel.app/?version=main>, which will use\n176\t   the latest main branch.\n177\t3. Or run _Black_ on your machine:\n178\t   - create a new virtualenv (make sure it's the same Python version);\n179\t   - clone this repository;\n180\t   - run `pip install -e .[d]`;\n181\t   - run `pip install -r test_requirements.txt`\n182\t   - make sure it's sane by running `python -m pytest`; and\n183\t   - run `black` like you did last time.\n184\t-->\n185\t\n186\t**Describe the bug**\n187\t\n188\t<!-- A clear and concise description of what the bug is. -->\n189\tWhen my code contains a multi-line expression that's concatenated using backslash (`\\`) and no indentation, black cannot parse my code\n190\t\n191\t**To Reproduce**\n192\t\n193\t<!--\n194\tMinimal steps to reproduce the behavior with source code and Black's configuration.\n195\t-->\n196\t\n197\tFor example, take this code:\n198\t\n199\t```python\n200\tif True:\n201\t    foo = 1+\\\n202\t2\n203\t    print(foo)\n204\t```\n205\t\n206\tAnd run it with these arguments:\n207\t\n208\t```sh\n209\t$ black file.py --target-version py313\n210\t```\n211\t\n212\tThe resulting error is:\n213\t\n214\t> error: cannot format file.py: Cannot parse for target version Python 3.13: 3:0: 2\n215\t\n216\t**Expected behavior**\n217\t\n218\t<!-- A clear and concise description of what you expected to happen. -->\n219\tThe file should be formatted to:\n220\t```\n221\tif True:\n222\t    foo = 1 + 2\n223\t    print(foo)\n224\t```\n225\t\n226\t**Environment**\n227\t\n228\t<!-- Please complete the following information: -->\n229\t\n230\t- Black's version: 25.12.0\n231\t- OS and Python version: Debian 13, Python (CPython) 3.14.2\n232\t\n233\t**Additional context**\n234\t\n235\t<!-- Add any other context about the problem here. -->\n236\t\n237\t\n238\t~~~~~~