verify_outputs	Compare requested and applied safe outputs	2026-10-21T18:05:03.5080433Z   AGENT_OUTPUT: {"items":[{"type":"add_labels","labels":["C: parser"]},{"type":"add_comment","body":"Thanks for the report! This is an automated first-pass triage; a maintainer will make the final call.\n\n**Reproduction:** Black 25.12.0 with `--target-version py313`, using the snippet from the report: parse error (`Cannot parse for target version Python 3.13: 3:0: 2`). This matches the report.\n**Assessment:** A backslash continuation may start its next line at any indentation, so the snippet is valid Python. The failure looks like a tokenizer/parser bug in Black's handling of a continuation line at column 0 inside an indented block. I found no matching earlier issue among the candidates.\n**Next step:** It would help to know whether the problem depends on the target version. Try the same file without `--target-version`, and with a different value such as `py312`, and report what you see.\n\n<sub>black-issue-triage skill v1.0.0 · suggested for maintainers: none</sub>","temporary_id":"aw_IA1MKGYy"}],"errors":[]}
